messages.content:
THOUGHT: The bug is in script.js: each click adds 2 to `count`, and displays `count - 1`, producing 1, 3, 5... instead of the true click count. I'll replace the click handler to increment `count` by 1 and display the real count, then verify with Playwright that after 3 clicks the displayed text is "3".

```mswea_bash_command
cat <<'EOF' > /home/user/app/script.js
let count = 0;

document.getElementById("increment").addEventListener("click", function () {
  count += 1;
  document.getElementById("count").textContent = String(count);
});
EOF
python3 -c "
from playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright
with sync_playwright() as p:
    page = p.chromium.launch().new_page()
    page.goto('file:///home/user/app/index.html')
    b = page.locator('#increment')
    for _ in range(3):
        b.click()
    print(page.locator('#count').inner_text())
"
```

